{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PiPancVhuEmrnukJn7zXPQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t+++\n2\tid = \"WI-589\"\n3\ttitle = \"Two verified defects around the one verdict definition: agent_loop's unpinned REVIEW_PHASES duplicate with its magic clamp, and IF-175's requestor list omitting scripts/score_reviews\"\n4\tworkstream = \"process\"\n5\tspecref = \"docs/requirements/interfaces.toml\"\n6\tbuildtier = \"strong\"\n7\tpriority = 3\n8\tsafety_class = \"spine\"\n9\tbar = \"DevStg-Tests\"\n10\t+++\n11\t\n12\t## Context\n13\t\n14\tDrafted by WI-586 (its ## Dispositions section) and minted at its merge - drafts-not-mints, ruling R1/R3.\n15\t\n16\tVERDICT THIS CONTINUES:\n17\t`docs/reviews/wi-586-adjudicate-llr-207-llr-208/009-ADJUDICATE-082b9e1.md`.\n18\tNeither defect is a fault in the four rows adjudicated there, so neither could be\n19\tcured by returning them; both were verified while reading their chain, and they\n20\tare queued rather than narrated because a finding recorded only in a file under\n21\t`docs/reviews/` is read by nothing — `gen_verdict_rollup` takes that file's\n22\tordinal, phase, sha, verdict word and finding COUNT, never its content.\n23\t\n24\t1. `agent_loop.py:317` declares `REVIEW_PHASES = (\"REVIEW-A\", \"REVIEW-B\")`, a\n25\t   byte-identical duplicate of `kitlib/verdict.py:157`, pinned by nothing; and\n26\t   `_clamped_review_rounds` (`:4160-4170`) clamps with a magic `min(2, rp_int)`\n27\t   whose `2` is that tuple's length restated as a literal. `IF-175`'s own notes\n28\t   argue the shared-definition case in as many words — \"there is exactly one\n29\t   definition, and a second reader of round evidence anywhere else is a finding\n30\t   against this row\". Import the constant and derive the clamp from its length,\n31\t   so a third phase cannot be added in one home and silently ignored in the\n32\t   other. This is the kit's own settled remedy (LLR-182's rationale: \"drift is\n33\t   better made unrepresentable than detected\").\n34\t2. `IF-175.requestors` is `[\"scripts/integrate\", \"scripts/agent_loop\",\n35\t   \"scripts/gen_verdict_rollup\"]`, but `scripts/score_reviews.py:72` holds a\n36\t   hard `from kitlib.verdict import declared_phases` and calls it at `:429`.\n37\t   By the row's own sentence that omission is \"a finding against this row\".\n38\t   Add the requestor, and state in the notes which half of the seam it reads\n39\t   (the declared phase span, not the round evidence) so the addition does not\n40\t   read as a fourth reader of the verdict.\n41\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36044c5c-57af-4ab0-8086-c83a51611ded","uuid":"060c9ca9-4d1c-456f-b2a6-095b273f5004","timestamp":"2026-09-03T23:12:56.947Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template-drive/wi-589-two-verified-defects-around-th/docs/work/active/wi-589-two-verified-defects-around-th/WI-589-two-verified-defects-around-th.md","content":"+++\nid = \"WI-589\"\ntitle = \"Two verified defects around the one verdict definition: agent_loop's unpinned REVIEW_PHASES duplicate with its magic clamp, and IF-175's requestor list omitting scripts/score_reviews\"\nworkstream = \"process\"\nspecref = \"docs/requirements/interfaces.toml\"\nbuildtier = \"strong\"\npriority = 3\nsafety_class = \"spine\"\nbar = \"DevStg-Tests\"\n+++\n\n## Context\n\nDrafted by WI-586 (its ## Dispositions section) and minted at its merge - drafts-not-mints, ruling R1/R3.\n\nVERDICT THIS CONTINUES:\n`docs/reviews/wi-586-adjudicate-llr-207-llr-208/009-ADJUDICATE-082b9e1.md`.\nNeither defect is a fault in the four rows adjudicated there, so neither could be\ncured by returning them; both were verified while reading their chain, and they\nare queued rather than narrated because a finding recorded only in a file under\n`docs/reviews/` is read by nothing — `gen_verdict_rollup` takes that file's\nordinal, phase, sha, verdict word and finding COUNT, never its content.\n\n1. `agent_loop.py:317` declares `REVIEW_PHASES = (\"REVIEW-A\", \"REVIEW-B\")`, a\n   byte-identical duplicate of `kitlib/verdict.py:157`, pinned by nothing; and\n   `_clamped_review_rounds` (`:4160-4170`) clamps with a magic `min(2, rp_int)`\n   whose `2` is that tuple's length restated as a literal. `IF-175`'s own notes\n   argue the shared-definition case in as many words — \"there is exactly one\n   definition, and a second reader of round evidence anywhere else is a finding\n   against this row\". Import the constant and derive the clamp from its length,\n   so a third phase cannot be added in one home and silently ignored in the\n   other. This is the kit's own settled remedy (LLR-182's rationale: \"drift is\n   better made unrepresentable than detected\").\n2. `IF-175.requestors` is `[\"scripts/integrate\", \"scripts/agent_loop\",\n   \"scripts/gen_verdict_rollup\"]`, but `scripts/score_reviews.py:72` holds a\n   hard `from kitlib.verdict import declared_phases` and calls it at `:429`.\n   By the row's own sentence that omission is \"a finding against this row\".\n   Add the requestor, and state in the notes which half of the seam it reads\n   (the declared phase span, not the round evidence) so the addition does not\n   read as a fourth reader of the verdict.\n","numLines":41,"startLine":1,"totalLines":41}}}
